{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520235993,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDMzNTIwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2257#issuecomment-370335206"},"message":"Structurally, these queries are pretty similar (content of unit that matches X and Y).\n\nFTR: Most of these queries require some kind of knowledge graph (any visual task, normally developing, autism, ...). DataLad will likely never compose such information, but should query such a graph that represents the current state of art for a given community. \n\nGiven the amount of queries necessary and their variability across dataset origins (communities), this list is evidence for an increasingly complex procedure to build a properly queriable body of information. This is the exact opposite direction of the one we where going over the past weeks (no index, no terms, simple matches of literal terms, instead of chunking/stemming/...). I guess this can serve as a guideline how much work should go into each search mode.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520620390,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTkwNTI2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2257#issuecomment-371905265"},"message":"\u003e queries require some kind of knowledge graph ... DataLad will likely never compose such information...\n\nFor starters -- Let's assume that such annotation (\"any visual task, normally developing, \") is available in BIDS datasets:  `group` column in participants.tsv for subject group, and task type as `CogAtlasID` in the _task.json file(s).   What usecases and how (with what search query) could then be answered?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520682904,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MjAyNDI1Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/dat